From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:02:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] h264_mvc: publish a picture only with both its views

The ISR pairs the two views of a picture by POC in the fill slot and
publishes the slot on a match. It never looked at which view arrived,
so the same view twice for one POC published the slot with the other
view's buffer id still -1. vf_get() then set no canvases, and the
vframe went out with those of the frame the slot carried before,
buffers the firmware may be decoding into again.

Publish the slot once it holds both views instead: a new picture starts
with one, so two means the second matched its POC. A view arriving again
for the picture replaces its buffer, as before, and the picture waits
for the other one.

The read-side check in vf_get() can no longer fail; it stays as a
one-time warning rather than going out silently with stale canvases.
The clean test, behind send_drop_cmd()'s count and the dirty flag, no
longer needs to test for both views.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h264_mvc/vh264_mvc.c b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h264_mvc/vh264_mvc.c
--- a/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h264_mvc/vh264_mvc.c
+++ b/drivers/frame_provider/decoder/h264_mvc/vh264_mvc.c
@@ -418,11 +418,10 @@
 	return stale;
 }
 
-/* both views there and neither dropped by the firmware */
+/* neither view dropped by the firmware */
 static bool vf_slot_clean(struct mvc_info_s *idx)
 {
-	return (idx->buf_id[0] >= 0) && (idx->buf_id[1] >= 0) &&
-		!idx->drop[0] && !idx->drop[1];
+	return !idx->drop[0] && !idx->drop[1];
 }
 
 static void set_frame_info(struct vframe_s *vf)
@@ -616,7 +615,7 @@
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&lock, flags);
 	vf = &vfpool[slot];
 
-	if ((view0_buf_id >= 0) && (view1_buf_id >= 0)) {
+	if (!WARN_ON_ONCE((view0_buf_id < 0) || (view1_buf_id < 0))) {
 		if (view_mode == 0 || view_mode == 1) {
 			vf->type = VIDTYPE_PROGRESSIVE | VIDTYPE_VIU_FIELD;
 
@@ -1233,8 +1232,9 @@
 			}
 			vf_slot_set_view(&vfpool_idx[slot], display_view_id,
 				display_buff_id, drop_status, stream_offset);
-			/* a POC match completes the picture */
-			complete = in_list_flag;
+			/* a new picture holds one view: both is a POC match */
+			complete = (vfpool_idx[slot].buf_id[0] >= 0) &&
+				(vfpool_idx[slot].buf_id[1] >= 0);
 			if (complete)
 				fill_slot = -1;
 			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&lock, flags);
